1
00:03:51,818 --> 00:03:57,818
The battle that changed the course of history.

2
00:07:43,636 --> 00:07:49,636
Wunderland is a action, war, drama film directed by Steven Luke.

3
00:11:35,454 --> 00:11:41,454
Christmas 1944, The Germans make one final push against
the attacking allied armies in the West.

4
00:15:27,272 --> 00:15:33,272
Robert Cappa and his platoon of 2nd Infantry Division soldiers have been
ordered to hold a vital road junction against the German aggressors.

5
00:19:19,090 --> 00:19:25,090
Cappa and his men must find their faith and strength to stand against their
enemy in the epic fight know as "The Battle of The Bulge."

6
00:23:10,909 --> 00:23:16,909
Sergeant McKeny, played by Jeremy Michael Pereira.

7
00:27:02,727 --> 00:27:08,727
Major McCulley, played by Tom Berenger.

8
00:30:54,545 --> 00:31:00,545
Lieutenant Cappa, played by Steven Luke.

9
00:34:46,363 --> 00:34:52,363
Captain Daniels, played by Aaron Courteau.

10
00:38:38,181 --> 00:38:44,181
Private Rudy, played by Cody Fleury.

11
00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:36,000
'Doc' Anderson, played by Andrew Stecker.

12
00:46:21,818 --> 00:46:27,818
The Miniatur Wunderland (German for: Miniature Wonderland) is, according to
Guinness World Records, the largest model railway system in the world.

13
00:50:13,636 --> 00:50:19,636
It is located at the historic Speicherstadt in Hamburg and is one of
the most popular and most visited sights in Germany.

14
00:54:05,454 --> 00:54:11,454
The exhibition includes around 1,230 digitally
controlled trains with more than 12,000 wagons.

15
00:57:57,272 --> 00:58:03,272
The Wonderland is also designed with around 5,280 houses and bridges, more than 11,800 vehicles – of which
around 350 drive independently on the installation – 52 airplanes and around 290,000 figures.

16
01:01:49,090 --> 01:01:55,090
The system features a recurring day-night lighting cycle
and almost 500,000 built-in LED lights.

17
01:05:40,909 --> 01:05:46,909
Of the 10,000 m2 (107,639 sq ft) of floorspace, the
models occupies 1,694 m2 (18,234 sq ft).

18
01:09:32,727 --> 01:09:38,727
As of May 2025, the railway consisted of 16,491 m (54,104 ft) of track in H0 scale with 3,600 switches and 1,400 signals, divided into twelve sections: Harz mountains, the fictitious
town of Knuffingen, the Alps and Austria, Hamburg, America, Scandinavia, Switzerland, a replica of Hamburg Airport, Italy, Rio de Janeiro, Patagonia and Monaco/Provence.

19
01:13:24,545 --> 01:13:30,545
Planning is also in progress for the construction of sections for
Central America and the Caribbean and perhaps Great Britain.

20
01:17:16,363 --> 01:17:22,363
The film explores themes of world war ii, battle of the bulge,
road battle, german army, american soldiers.

21
01:21:08,181 --> 01:21:14,181
The tone is emotional and intense.
